>Funny, I thought the unix Makefiles are used in bsd.

They are.  However, each port has its own makefile, which draws largely
from a skeleton.  That file can then fetch the source, extract the code
in ./work, apply patches, and only then does it pass control to the
applications own Makefile.  

>> There just isn't an "update" target in the port makefiles.  Ports are
>> updated, whether manually or automatically, by "make deinstall" to
>> remove the old, and then "make install" for the new.

>Does the install target somehow check that the deinstall is made?
